{
  "_comment": [
    "Market keyword taxonomy for NEW-COMPETITOR DISCOVERY.",
    "",
    "These are category terms, not brand names. They are used to find products",
    "entering the space — not to count mentions of the 7 tracked products.",
    "",
    "PRIORITY drives the rotation. A full sweep of every keyword is far more",
    "queries than the rate-limited search backend can serve in one run, so the",
    "collector walks a persisted cursor and covers the list over successive runs.",
    "Higher-priority categories are visited more often because they surface",
    "product lists directly:",
    "",
    "  3 = surfaces named products almost every time ('best X', 'X alternative')",
    "  2 = surfaces products often, mixed with editorial",
    "  1 = mostly editorial; scanned least frequently",
    "",
    "`discovery_value` records WHY a category earns its priority, so the weighting",
    "is auditable rather than arbitrary."
  ],
  "categories": [
